Cell[TextData[{
 "Kuiper2sample implements the exact algorithm of Proposition 2 and Remark \
2.3 of Dimitrova, Jia, Kaishev (2026), which extends the Nikiforov (1994) \
recurrence to handle the joint one-sided bounds needed for the Kuiper \
statistic. Prior exact formulas (Maag and Stephens 1968; Hirakawa 1973) \
required equal sample sizes and continuous data. This implementation handles \
arbitrary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "a62da658-848a-2648-86bb-83f4310545fd"],
 " and tied observations. \nThe kuiperks helper function uses a boundary \
offset of 10\:207b\:2079 in DEVIATUP and DEVIATDOWN. This enforces the strict \
inequality convention (D\:207a < a, D\:207b < b) consistent with the original \
Nikiforov Fortran code and its C++/R descendants. Removing it would cause \
off-by-one errors at lattice boundary values of q."
}], "Text",
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellEventActions->{Inherited, {"KeyDown", "\t"} :> Replace[SelectionMove[
       SelectedNotebook[], After, Cell]; NotebookFind[
       SelectedNotebook[], "TabNext", Next, CellTags, AutoScroll -> True, 
       WrapAround -> True], Blank[NotebookSelection] :> SelectionMove[
       SelectedNotebook[], All, CellContents, AutoScroll -> True]], 
   PassEventsDown -> False, PassEventsUp -> False},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990020789708439*^9, 3.9900208377603664`*^9}},
 CellTags->{"DefaultContent", "TabNext"},
 CellID->908162033,ExpressionUUID->"93298da8-b35b-7c46-9213-0843757b3c29"]
}, Open  ]],

